          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ફરજ (pharaj) is a loan from Arabic farḍ, \"obligation\", which reached Gujarati through Persian farz (EtymDB). Its Arabic root is f-r-ḍ (Lane)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
